    {
      "id": "s9",
      "short": "Cache fleet",
      "title": "Case: growing a cache cluster",
      "chapter": "insight",
      "body": "A fleet of Memcached servers sits in front of a database, and clients pick a server with `hash(key) % N`. Adding a fifth server remaps ~80% of keys — they all miss at once, and the database is flattened by the stampede.\n\nWith consistent hashing, adding the fifth server moves only ~20% of keys. The cache stays mostly warm and the database barely notices.",
      "callout": {
        "kind": "insight",
        "text": "This is where consistent hashing started: spreading web caches across machines that come and go."
      },
      "changes": [
        "+ Fifth cache server",
        "~ Cache misses after the change: 80% → 20%"
      ],
      "metrics": {
