    {
      "id": "s10",
      "short": "Recap",
      "title": "Recap",
      "chapter": "recap",
      "body": "• Put servers and keys on a **hash ring**; a key belongs to the **next server clockwise**.\n• Adding or removing a server moves only **one arc** — about 1/N of keys.\n• **Virtual nodes** even out shares and spread the load when servers leave.\n• Store each key on the **next N servers** clockwise for redundancy.",
      "callout": {
        "kind": "tip",
        "text": "Next up: **Unique IDs at Scale** — giving every row a name once there is no single database to count for you."
      },
